# Scorecard kiosk - Wi-Fi credentials.
#
# Copy to the FAT boot partition as: wifi-credentials
# (on a running unit that is /boot/firmware/wifi-credentials)
#
# Why this file exists rather than relying on NetworkManager's own store:
# an unclean power loss can leave NM's profile files zero-length. ext4's journal
# protects metadata, not file contents, so the filesystem comes back "clean"
# while the credentials inside it are gone. A headless unit that has forgotten
# its Wi-Fi password cannot be reached to fix it - the SD card has to come out.
#
# The FAT boot partition is written to almost never, so it survives that.
# wifi-selfheal.service reads this on every boot and rebuilds the NetworkManager
# profile if none exists. This file is the single source of truth: if the
# network changes, edit here.
#
# Quote the SSID - it may contain spaces.
#
# SECURITY: this is the Wi-Fi passphrase in plain text on a partition readable
# by anyone holding the SD card. See "Security notes" in README.md before
# shipping units into customer networks.

WIFI_SSID="YOUR_WIFI_SSID"
WIFI_PSK="YOUR_WIFI_PASSPHRASE"
